@* Spam trap for a public enquiry form. Render it inside the <form>. The field is moved off screen
   (not display:none, which some bots skip), hidden from screen readers and left out of the tab
   order, so people never fill it in; bots that fill every field do. The page model needs
   [Honeypot], and its handler must skip saving when HoneypotAttribute.Caught(HttpContext). *@
<div class="honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
    <label for="@($"hp-{OptimumEarth.Web.Services.HoneypotAttribute.FieldName}")">Leave this field empty</label>
    <input type="text" id="@($"hp-{OptimumEarth.Web.Services.HoneypotAttribute.FieldName}")" name="@OptimumEarth.Web.Services.HoneypotAttribute.FieldName" value="" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
</div>
